| `tests.memory_scratch_root` | string or null | `/dev/shm/<project_slug>-tests`: `/dev/shm/my_project-tests` by default, `/dev/shm/project_keel-tests` in keel; absent, null, which its reader reports as `[using default] tests.memory_scratch_root = null` | an absolute path with no `..` part in a memory-backed directory, never under the system temporary directory or inside the checkout; null | `tests/isolation_guard.py` (`choose_scratch`), called by `tests/conftest.py` at import, through `scripts/config_loader.py`'s `tests.memory_scratch_root` row | Makes memory the first choice for test scratch when `KEEL_TEST_SCRATCH` is unset: the session uses this path with `-<uid>` appended, made with mode 0700, when its parent exists and is not writable by other users without the sticky bit, its file system has `tests.memory_scratch_min_free_mb` free, and the directory is one this user owns with mode 0700; otherwise `tests.scratch_root`. A link at the configured name is never followed, and a trailing `/` is dropped. pytest's `scratch:` header line, which `-q` hides, names the root in use and why memory was passed over. Null turns memory off. A refused value stops pytest before any test runs (exit 4), naming this key. | a cap on what scratch may hold: a session's kept directories count against the memory, bounded by `pyproject.toml` `tmp_path_retention_count` | always |
